errors.edited_files:
{count} deploy file(s) were edited by hand, and the update would overwrite them:
{diffs}
Move each edit into {file} (yours: no release writes it, and every compose command reads it), delete the edited file, and retry; the release's copy is written in its place.

errors.restore_needed_external:
{current} goes back to {target} without a restore only when {target} is its rollback_to, and it is not: {current} may have migrated the database past what {target} reads.

  thulu update -to {target} -restore {snapshot}

Restore your database to the snapshot taken before the update to {current} first; -restore external says you did.
